John Stephen Haro wrote:
> 
> Anyone have a chuck of a .login script for DUX4.0D they can zing me that
> will set the DISPLAY variable automatically on remote login?
> 

The following (korn/bash) script works for me,
across all the common platforms.

Are you really still using csh? - Translation
left as an exercise for the reader.

The who in /usr/local/bin would be the gnu one.
As it is one of those code fragments that, like topsy, just grow,
It could probably be greatly improved.

Hope this helps

---------<cut here>---------------------
if [ -z "$DISPLAY" ]
then
    if [ `which who` = "/usr/local/bin/who" ]
    then
            DISPLAY=`who am i`
    else
        case `uname` in
        HP-UX)
            DISPLAY=`who -R am i`
            ;;
        OSF1)
            DISPLAY=`who -M am i`
            ;;
        *)
            DISPLAY=`who am i`
        esac
    fi

    DISPLAY=`IFS="()" ; set $DISPLAY; echo $2`

    case `uname` in
    AIX|Linux)
        # truncated to 16 chars, so strip off domain
        DISPLAY=`echo $DISPLAY | sed 's/\..*//'`
        ;;
    esac

    DISPLAY=$DISPLAY:0.0
    export DISPLAY

    echo "export DISPLAY=$DISPLAY"
fi
---------<cut here>---------------------

-- 
Alan J. Wylie (Cyrano UK Ltd.) | mailto:awylie@cyrano.com
http://www.cyrano.com          | http://www.zen.co.uk/home/page/alan.wylie
