Hi

We have just taken delivery of a new Alpha Workstation, which had been
pre-configured but the keyboard wasn't working correctly.  The language
was set to 38 English(American), whereas we wanted 36 English(British). 
At the chevron prompt I went to type:
	set language 36
but foolishly hit return, before typing 36.  As a result the language
has been set to some weird and wonderful number and the functionality of
the keyboard is nothing like it should be.  Now, when we reboot we are
offered the chance to select a language from a menu which is all well
and good but typing in our selection is impossible given our situation.

Is there any way to reset the language to the factory setting, or is
this a case for the engineer ?

Thanks
	Matt.
